## CHECKED AND CLEARED (not merges)

- **CH.KM.21a / CH.KM.21a.3** (2 francs): 21a has 5 specimens and catalogs KM#21a.1 — this is a **rename** (CH.KM.21a → CH.KM.21a.1), not a merge. 21a.3 (1991) is a legitimate sub-variety; keep separate.
- **CH.KM.40a.1 / CH.KM.40a.4** (5 francs): different designs/eras (1978 vs 2014). Keep separate.
- **CH.KM.26 / CH.KM.26c** (5 rappen): sub-variety split. Keep separate.
- **DE.KM.109.1 / DE.KM.109.2** (50 pfennig): composition variants. Keep separate.
- **ES.KM.1040 / ES.KM.1144, FR.KM.1285 / FR.KM.1410, NL.KM.236 / NL.KM.346** (euro): portrait redesign series. Keep separate.
- **GB.KM.935 / 935a, GB.KM.1109 / 1109d, GB.KM.1110 / 1110d** (etc.): portrait/metal series. Keep separate.
- **GT.KM.239.2 / GT.KM.277.1, KY.KM.132 / KY.KM.88a, MX-CHI.KM.612 / MX.KM.424, NL.KM.107.2 / NL.KM.170**: different eras/designs. Keep separate.
- **FR.KM.888b.1 / FR.X.5-francs**: 1946 Lavrillier vs 1994 — different types entirely. FR.X.5-francs just needs a KM# (likely KM#1021), not a merge.
- **MX.KM.433 / MX.X.10-centavos**: 1945 vs 1995 — different types. Keep separate.

